# Assets and rights

- Never assume a conversion, pixelization, slicing, or AI tool grants rights to its source.
- Every imported asset needs a stable ID, provenance/rights record, source hash, dimensions, pivot, atlas group, and runtime path.
- Source exports live under `art/imports`; runtime output is generated.
- Do not hand-edit generated atlases.
- Validate alpha, frame bounds, naming, padding, and nearest-neighbor appearance.
- For GPU layers, group compatible frames into a single texture and account for power-of-two/padding constraints.
- Run `pnpm assets:validate` after manifest changes.
